ns transmit information  from the physical world into our brains  we then analyzed the information and  form conclusions however every piece of  information is received by sense organs  that no one else can have in the exact  same form in the exact same place at the  exact same time on one's evaluation of  the sensory information is entirely  based on their unique prior  understanding of the world no one can  ever be in your head and truly see the  world from your perspective just like  you can never be in anyone else's and so  one's experience of reality is and will  always be subjected not only that but  our sensory perception is constantly  being tricked by the outside world  making us experience things that aren't  always there or miss things that are all  of this raises the following in order  for something to be observed like the  universe it needs an observer but an  observer requires a means of observation  like sensory organs and a conscious  brain to make discernments but how can  something observe while not being  limited to the conditions of its means  of observation it can't this raises at  least two possible answers to the  questioning if anything is objective  real either there is an objective truth  to the nature of everything which is  indifferent to observation but current  humanity can simply not access it or  nothing is objectively real and what  appears real is relative to the nature  and abilities of the observing party all  we have is our own brain and we can  never experience the world from outside  it according to the concept of the  egocentric predicament this means  everything outside of one's brain is  impossible to ever prove as real or not  all we can do is hope that at least  something is it's clear that no matter  how far we have come or how smart and  powerful we may feel we're still  embryonic in the birth of knowledge and  understanding there is mystery every  time we go to bed and every time we wake  up every time we perceive something  every time we make a decision every time  we think about the world or the universe  or ourself the fact that we are aware  enough to ask questions and self-honest  enough to admit when we don't know the  answers is a testament to the beauty of  being human perhaps being a human is to  reside somewhere in the space between  knowing and unknowing a space that  allows us to speculate consider learn  and create stories art and videos like  these to have something incredible to  talk about with lovers friends and  family arguably to be human is the most  fascinating experience in the history of  the universe not because we have all the  answers but because we will always have  enough to ask about the ones we don't  or maybe we'll find all the answers one  day and then life will be even better  who knows  thank you for watching if he found  enjoyment and value in this video please  give it a thumbs up share your thoughts  in the comments below and if you are not  already be sure to subscribe to our  channel we are constantly coming out  with new videos to help you experience  life with clarity and Wonder
 

